# Fraction Compressor: environment template.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and fill in your own key ONLY if you want to
# call the Meta Model API the way this project did during the event:
# Muse Spark designed the compression recipes and checked the claims.
# That loop ran through external tooling during the event, not through
# a script in this repo; everything it produced (recipes, held-out
# questions, judging records) is committed under results/.
#
# Nothing else in this repository needs a key. The compressor, the
# quickstart, the patch maker, the hot-swap demo, and the benchmark
# reruns all work with no API key at all: they read the recipes and
# result files already in the repo.
#
# Get a key from the Meta Model API console at https://dev.meta.ai
# (API keys). The endpoint is https://api.meta.ai/v1 and the model used
# for recipe design and claim-checking is muse-spark-1.3.
#
# Never commit a filled-in .env file.
META_MODEL_API_KEY=your-meta-model-api-key-here

# Optional: during the event the same recipe and judging prompts were
# also run against Muse Spark Open hosted on Baseten and on Fireworks,
# as cross-checks. Keys for those hosts, if you want to call them the
# same way:
# BASETEN_API_KEY=your-baseten-api-key-here
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY=your-fireworks-api-key-here
